Map data (optional modules in maps/, not part of the library bundle)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
maps/world.js, maps/world.json - 177 countries, 1:110m
  Geometry: world-atlas 2.0.2 (countries-110m.json), Copyright 2013-2019
  Michael Bostock, ISC License; derived from Natural Earth.
  Attributes (name, ISO 3166 codes, continent, subregion): Natural Earth
  1:110m Cultural Vectors, Admin 0 - Countries. Natural Earth is in the
  public domain (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/).
maps/world-small-states.js, maps/world-small-states.json - optional 185-region map
  Retains the above 177-region 1:110m geometry and adds actual 1:10m boundaries
  for AND, BHR, LIE, MCO, MLT, SGP, SMR and VAT from Natural Earth
  ne_10m_admin_0_countries.geojson (public domain), official source commit
  ca96624a56bd078437bca8184e78163e5039ad19. Selected source features, the full
  source SHA-256, pinned URL and regeneration instructions are preserved in
  maps/source/natural-earth-small-states.geojson and maps/SMALL-STATES.md.
  This optional supplement does not claim complete ISO country/territory coverage.
maps/us-states.js, maps/us-states.json - 50 states, DC and territories, 1:10m
  Geometry: us-atlas 3.0.1 (states-10m.json), Copyright 2013-2019 Michael Bostock,
  ISC License; derived from US Census Bureau cartographic boundary files
  (public domain).
Sources are kept in maps/source/; tools/build-maps.js trims properties,
drops unused objects/arcs and writes the modules (about 40 kB gzipped each).
Only data files were taken from these packages; no code from them is used.
The TopoJSON decoder, antimeridian cutting and projections (Equal Earth:
Savric, Patterson & Jenny 2018; Albers / Mercator: Snyder 1987) are our own
implementations in src/premium/map/geo.js.

